{
  "version": "V0.29.58",
  "theme": "US-792 -- re-arm shutdown latch after a cancel",
  "description": "Ships the Sprint 89 payload with the latch defect it exposed. firedAlready is set on all three exits of handleOnBattery, incl. cancel, and nothing reset it -- so a blip that cancelled a shutdown left the trigger dead for the whole boot and the next key-off was a hard cut. _runPldWatchLoop now clears it on the tick the PLD line reads present, no debounce. Also carries US-767 EDR drive-coupling."
}
